## tsconfig.json (Optional)

> **Note**
>
> SmartGen Showcase **does not strictly require TypeScript** out of the box. This configuration file is **optional** and is provided as a reference for developers.
>
> However, because showcase sites often rely on interactive visual elements, this file is highly recommended if you plan to add custom client-side features, such as:
>
> - Interactive gallery filtering (e.g., sorting UI kits vs. templates)
> - Dynamic lightbox and modal popups for images
> - Custom theme switchers (Dark/Light mode)
> - Advanced CSS grid masonry layouts via JavaScript
> - Custom animations for design assets
>
> If your showcase project only uses **Python, HTML, CSS, Jinja2, and Markdown**, you can safely ignore or remove this file.

{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "Node",

    "strict": true,

    "allowJs": false,

    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,

    "sourceMap": true,

    "removeComments": false,

    "declaration": false,

    "skipLibCheck": true,

    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,

    "isolatedModules": true,

    "noEmitOnError": true,

    "lib": [
      "DOM",
      "DOM.Iterable",
      "ES2022"
    ],

    "outDir": "./dist",

    "rootDir": "./src",

    "types": [
      "node"
    ]
  },

  "include": [
    "src/**/*.ts"
  ],

  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "site"
  ]
}
